All you can tell from this error message is that you are missing ram.  
Say you are in the situation that you are using 1.9 GB and then try  
to create an object of 200MB. Then the error will be "cannot allocate  
vector of size 200MB", so you are probably using way more memory.

It seems like you are reading in some big output files. This may be  
made possible by changing the reading routine to a function that is  
less memory hungry. Or you might simply have to little RAM. I suggest  
contacting the authors of BGX. It seems pretty silly that an output  
analysis of a MCMC run stored on disk should be so memory hungry - of  
course that depends on what they are doing.

Kasper


