From rgentlem at fhcrc.org  Sat Jan 26 06:27:01 2008
From: rgentlem at fhcrc.org (Robert Gentleman)
Date: Fri, 25 Jan 2008 21:27:01 -0800
Subject: [BioC] dumb question: using Biostrings (or something else)	to
 translate DNA bases to amino acid codes
In-Reply-To: <1201324224.479ac0c00aae2@webmail.fhcrc.org>
References: <875A97EF-F3F1-4BCA-9897-7A3A984B7EBF@systemsbiology.org>
	<1201324224.479ac0c00aae2@webmail.fhcrc.org>
Message-ID: <479AC4A5.6090507@fhcrc.org>

for reasonably short sequences (like most genes)

library(Biostrings)
  DNA2AA = function(DNAseq) {
     if(length(DNAseq) > 1 ) stop("only length one sequences, please")
     nc = nchar(DNAseq)
     Dtriples = substring(DNAseq, seq(1, nc, by=3), seq(3, nc, 3))
     paste(GENETIC_CODE[Dtriples], collapse="")
  }

  will do it. The restriction to length one sequences is due to the 
semantics of substring

  best wishes
    Robert



